#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:5
#: 359d8b859e7a4f548c79eda90c3857de
msgid "Servo Gripper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:7
#: b85009c2c00f470996110daeadfd8382
msgid "This article explains how to connect a servo to an autopilot and configure it for use as a gripper which is useful for delivery or bottle drop applications. The servo can be controlled directly by the pilot via a switch on the transmitter or as part of a mission.  You may wish to refer to the :ref:`general servo wiki page <common-servo>` for other ways servos can be controlled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:14
#: 00e5f4fe40dc421c9a82c66264ecebdf
msgid "Connecting the servo to an autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:19
#: 342cbea317b74b48a9647152e76a67be
msgid "If using Copter, connect the servo to AUX OUT 1, 2, 3 or 4 if the autopilot includes an IOMCU for the first 8 MAIN outputs, or any output operating at 50Hz if the autopilot does not use an IOMCU.  MAIN OUT 1 ~ 8 should be avoided because these normally update at 400hz.  If using Plane or Rover where all PWM output pins usually update at 50hz, any unused output may be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:20
#: 5ebc338c9b2749b79bcf71b03f103681
msgid "In some autopilots with IOMCUs, AUX OUT 5 and 6 cannot be used by default because they are setup by default as :ref:`Relays <common-relay>`.  These pins can changed to Servo outputs by setting the ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` parameter to 6 and setting :ref:`RELAY2_PIN<RELAY2_PIN>` and :ref:`RELAY1_PIN<RELAY1_PIN>` to -1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:21
#: d506d3ebb969497eb8dd8e8dcf3a0b23
msgid "If the autopilot cannot provide power to the servos, an external BEC or ESC that can provide 5V should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:24
#: 858337aedef749f481f47c9f756adfc8
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:25
#: afe1b9a5a3194a79a60cb485e6b00028
msgid "set which RC output is used by setting SERVOx_FUNCTION (or RCX_FUNCTION) to 28 (i.e. if using AUX OUT 1 on a Pixhawk, set :ref:`SERVO9_FUNCTION <SERVO9_FUNCTION>` to 28)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:26
#: 1f48de660d74490cb91f6fa1c5791ea0
msgid ":ref:`GRIP_ENABLE <GRIP_ENABLE>` to 1 to enable the gripper feature and then refetch parameters from the ground station in order to make other gripper parameters visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:27
#: b37d2ea375f64fc5918514c0fdfa9e26
msgid ":ref:`GRIP_TYPE <GRIP_TYPE>` to 1 to enable the servo gripper and reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:28
#: 935f7e1ad9504c8ebff62d823ce69380
msgid ":ref:`GRIP_GRAB <GRIP_GRAB>` to the pwm value (i.e. 1000 ~ 2000) for the gripper's closed position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:29
#: c4478b60adf14fb281f019a98686d797
msgid ":ref:`GRIP_RELEASE <GRIP_RELEASE>` to the pwm value for the gripper's open position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:30
#: 2f09e3e91e2043bf95324687e9123941
msgid ":ref:`GRIP_NEUTRAL <GRIP_NEUTRAL>` to the pwm value for the gripper's neutral position (often the same as its closed position)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:33
#: 9bf329cac8124f9a96bccfe52765218c
msgid "Controlling Gripper from the transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:35
#: 35ad924677c44139a4b025555460d72d
msgid "One of the transmitter's auxiliary switches can control the gripper by setting an ``RCx_OPTION`` parameter to \"19\" (Gripper)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:38
#: eae7a261680646a6aa801195891a446e
msgid "Controlling Gripper during a mission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:40
#: 80b2ac07926048c9a962a4cc55774328
msgid "The gripper position can be controlled during a mission in AUTO mode using the :ref:`DO_GRIPPER <common-mavlink-mission-command-messages-mav_cmd>` command.  Set the \"drop/grab\" column to 0 to drop (open the gripper), 1 to grab (close the gripper)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:46
#: 4e29a822a782425396a678f0d06a43b7
msgid "Controlling Gripper from the ground station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-gripper-servo.rst:48
#: 10471ba4494349cfa92ab947ffcd93ef
msgid "The gripper can be opened or closed in real-time from the ground station if the ground station sends a `COMMAND_LONG <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#COMMAND_LONG>`__ with the command field set to DO_GRIPPER (i.e. 211) but there are no ground stations (as far as we know) that support doing this."
msgstr ""
